# shadcn (admin + web)

When building or changing UI in `apps/admin` or `apps/web`, use the shadcn
components already in `src/components/ui` (Base UI, Tailwind CSS v4). Add more
with `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name> -c apps/<app>`.

For `apps/web`, also read `DESIGN.md` and open `docs/reference-app.png` before
building UI. The web theme tokens in `src/app/[locale]/globals.css` already map
those colors. `apps/admin` stays on the neutral shadcn theme and does not follow
that consumer visual language.

Patterns:

- Prefer the local shadcn components (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `Dialog`, `Table`, and so on)
- Style with Tailwind utilities and theme tokens (`text-muted-foreground`, `bg-card`, `gap-4`)
- Links that look like buttons use `buttonVariants()` on the locale `Link`. Do not pass a link through `Button`
- `cn` comes from the `cn` package
- Do not add Material UI, Emotion, Gluestack, UniWind, React Native Paper, or react-native-web
- Component placement (see CLAUDE.md): shared → `src/components/`; route-only →
  `app/.../<route>/components/`. Reuse existing components instead of duplicating.

Mobile UI rules live in `.cursor/rules/expo-mobile-ui.mdc` and `CLAUDE.md`.
